    "sha": "5ada1a9231533e97e5d0562c3735d3d6041e26be",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDVhZGExYTkyMzE1MzNlOTdlNWQwNTYyYzM3MzVkM2Q2MDQxZTI2YmU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T23:51:35Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T23:51:35Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(motion): the scallop law's reach ceiling - a stepover at the ball diameter is refused\n\nThe ridge flank law reads a cusp only to 4*tol past the ball (s ~ 2.9 on\nan r3 ball), and the 3D finish door accepted any positive stepover, so a\nspacing past that verified silent on scallop. The generator now refuses,\nby name, a stated stepover or steep stepover at or past the ball diameter\n(past s = 2r the cusp formula h = r - sqrt(r^2 - (s/2)^2) describes uncut\nground, not a cusp) and a tolerance at or past r/2 (where the auto law\nsqrt(8 r tol) reaches 2r). The scan's reach stays band + 3*tol with its\nvalidity range documented: a 2r far tier was built and measured, and it\nconvicted the cone apex, box walls and dome crown (11 verdict-lane tests),\nso it waits on a crown/corner exclusion (RECOMMENDED \"#37\").\n\nPinned by scallop_ceiling (at / just under / past the diameter and r/2,\ndegenerate radius and tolerance); the authored-ladder test moves from\nsteep_stepover 8 to 5 on the 6 mm ball.\n\nFixes #37\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
